VALUES ('ENG-001', 'BS Agricultural and Biosystems Engineering', 'Engineering & Technology', 'INTERNATIONAL', 'Moderate', ARRAY['Canada', 'Australia', 'USA'], TRUE, 'Agricultural Engineer Licensure Exam', 5, 'Target Canadian agri-food companies under NOC 21399 and pursue a PEng pathway via Engineers Canada after 4 years of Canadian work experience.', 'Philippines Washington Accord membership (2023) strengthens credential recognition for ABET-accredited programs. Strong fit for Canada''s agri-food tech sector and Australia''s precision agriculture industry.')
