VALUES ('HLT-006', 'BS Nutrition and Dietetics', 'Health Professions', 'INTERNATIONAL', 'Moderate', ARRAY['USA', 'Canada', 'Australia', 'UK', 'UAE'], TRUE, 'Nutritionist-Dietitian Licensure Exam', 4, 'The PRC-CDR Reciprocity Agreement is a unique advantage — prioritize 2 years of post-licensure experience to qualify for US RD exam pathway.', 'Philippines has a formal CDR (Commission on Dietetic Registration) Reciprocity Agreement with the USA — RND holders with 2 years experience can take the US RD Exam (CDR). This is a significant advantage. Canada requires credential evaluation + Dietetic Qualifying Exam. Australia requires DAA accreditation or bridging. Gulf countries recruit clinical dietitians for hospitals. Growing demand globally driven by diabetes, obesity, and aging populations.')
